---
import Content from '../layouts/Content.astro';
import ThermalArchitecture from '../components/ThermalArchitecture.astro';
import { company, site, power, solar } from '../data/site';
const serviceKva = Math.round(Math.sqrt(3) * 208 * 3000 / 1000);
---
<Content
  title={`Power and cooling for phased AI infrastructure | ${company.full}`}
  description={`${power.utility} serves the on-site ${power.service} transformer at ${site.designation}. Explore the commissioning target, proposed two-loop cooling, and planned solar and storage.`}
  kicker="Power and cooling"
  heading="Infrastructure for the next phase."
  lede={`The campus starts with an on-site ${power.service} transformer supplied by ${power.utility}. Construction, electrical commissioning and cooling are coordinated around the first compute deployment in Buildings A and C.`}
  meta={[
    { label: 'Utility', value: power.utility, note: 'On-site transformer', tone: 'gold' },
    { label: 'Shared service', value: power.service, note: power.serviceScope },
    { label: 'Commissioning', value: power.commissioningTarget, note: 'Management target; not completed', tone: 'signal' },
    { label: 'Planned energy', value: `${solar.tractAcres} acres`, note: 'Tract 3, solar and storage' },
  ]}
>
  <section aria-labelledby="service" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">01</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Electrical infrastructure</span></p>
    <h2 id="service">Transformer on site. Commissioning ahead.</h2>
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <p>The on-site transformer and shared distribution serve Buildings A, B and C. Buildings A and C provide {site.dataCenterArea.toLocaleString()} gross sq ft for data-center development; Building B supports batteries, utilities and storage.</p>
        <p>{site.contractor} is the construction contractor, with a {site.constructionTarget}. The electrical commissioning milestone is an {power.commissioningTarget}. These management targets are part of the development schedule; customer service begins after equipment, cooling and connectivity are ready.</p>
      </div>
      <dl class="spec">
        <div><dt>Serving utility</dt><dd>{power.utility}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>On-site transformer</dt><dd>{power.service}<span class="note">One shared service across Buildings A, B and C.</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Apparent service rating</dt><dd>Approximately {serviceKva.toLocaleString()} kVA<span class="note">Calculated from stated voltage and current. This is not an available IT allocation.</span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>House / office</dt><dd>{power.houseOfficeService}<span class="note">Separate from the data-center building allocation.</span></dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
    <div class="callout" style="margin-top: var(--s-6);">
      <p><strong>Capacity for your deployment.</strong> We size each customer allocation against the electrical design, cooling system and commissioned operating limits. Share your IT load and redundancy requirements to start that review.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <ThermalArchitecture />
  <section aria-labelledby="solar" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">02</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Energy development</span></p>
    <h2 id="solar">Solar and storage, alongside compute.</h2>
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <p>{solar.publicCopy}</p>
        <p>{company.parent}, the parent battery producer, connects the campus strategy with energy-storage development. SmartTec.dev LLC operates under SmartTec Holdings LLC, bringing data-center operations into that wider platform.</p>
        <p>Solar and storage are a planned development phase. Equipment sizing, utility approval and commissioning will establish the contribution they can make to the campus.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Three connected uses</h3>
        <ul class="bullets">
          <li>Buildings A and C: compute and colocation.</li>
          <li>Building B: batteries, utilities and storage.</li>
          <li>Tract 3: planned solar and energy storage.</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/site">Explore the campus →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="is-end" aria-labelledby="deployment" data-reveal>
    <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true"><span class="eyebrow__n">03</span><span class="eyebrow__t">Your requirements</span></p>
    <h2 id="deployment">Plan the load, cooling and service together.</h2>
    <p>A deployment proposal brings together IT power, cooling, metering, support and commercial terms. Include your uptime and compliance requirements so they can be assessed before an offer. No commissioned capacity or uptime guarantee is advertised at this development stage.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="btn" href="/contact">Discuss your deployment</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/compute">Explore planned compute</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Content>
